  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Since the angles $∠AJI$ and $∠CIF$ are corresponding angles, they are congruent and therefore have the same measure:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠AJI & =m∠CIF \\\\ 3x & ={75}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have an equation that we can solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x & ={75}^{∘} \\\\ \\frac{3x}{3} & =\\frac{{75}^{∘}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{3}x}{\\cancel{3}} & ={25}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={25}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
